    "mainline_role": "Use v11 as evidence that the L2 transaction can contain a typed post-step physical observer signal. Keep L1 semantic alignment, L2 exact dispatch/effect binding, and the prevention-versus-containment boundary as the paper mainline; do not market v11 as a complete defense.",
    "official_endpoint_result": "Official cost/collision counts do not show a consistent arm ordering, so v11 does not establish overall physical safety.",
    "positive_system_claim": "Across clean and attacked pilots, 16 model-defined joint-limit triggers were bound into L2 evidence and no later action was dispatched in those episodes.",
    "risk_result": "Aggregate joint-limit step burden is sharply lower in L2-enabled arms in both conditions, while paired sign tests remain underpowered and non-confirmatory.",
    "utility_result": "Observed paired task-success differences are -13.33pp and -6.67pp in clean, and -6.67pp and -6.67pp under attack; exact paired tests do not establish superiority or noninferiority."
